From a6a01b777b051fee7628a50dec59fe627b4fb947 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 09:59:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/15] feat(build-image): auto-sync Marathon-Image device
 aports into pmaports
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

mkosi's sandbox bind-mounts the duranium source dir but its
follow-symlinks logic dangles when targets point outside the bind
root. Marathon's per-device overlay aports (device-purism-librem5-
marathon, device-oneplus-enchilada-marathon, ...) were symlinks from
pmaports/device/community/ into $MARATHON_IMAGE_DIR/packages/, which
meant the symlinks resolved on the host but were broken inside the
sandbox — pmaports.py's deviceinfo resolver couldn't read the
APKBUILD to walk the depends chain. Pi 5 worked only because its
overlay aport happened to have been replaced with a real directory
at some earlier point.

Fix: at the top of build_image(), rsync every Marathon-Image
device-*-marathon aport into pmaports/device/community/<same name>/,
overwriting any existing copy (whether symlink or real-dir snapshot).
Source-of-truth is $MARATHON_IMAGE_DIR/packages/; pmaports gets a
just-in-time snapshot every build. New aports auto-flow through too.

Caught while diagnosing Librem 5 build attempt 1 — the resolver
errored with "deviceinfo not found" inside the sandbox even though
the aport was visible on the host.
---
 scripts/build-image.py | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/scripts/build-image.py b/scripts/build-image.py
index 954aa95..6f66192 100755
--- a/scripts/build-image.py
+++ b/scripts/build-image.py
@@ -63,6 +63,36 @@ def build_image(components: List[str], extra_args: List[str]):
         print(f"Device: {device_name}, UI: {ui_name}")
         print(f"ImageID: {image_id}")
 
+        # Sync Marathon-Image device overlay aports into pmaports/community/
+        # so mkosi.configure's resolver can see them inside the sandbox.
+        # mkosi's bind-mount follows symlinks but the symlink targets point
+        # outside the sandbox root and dangle inside, so we copy. JIT here
+        # so the latest Marathon-Image edits flow through every build.
+        # Source-of-truth remains $MARATHON_IMAGE_DIR/packages/.
+        marathon_image_dir = os.environ.get(
+            "MARATHON_IMAGE_DIR",
+            os.path.expanduser("~/Developer/Marathon-Image"),
+        )
+        pmaports_community = os.path.join("pmaports", "device", "community")
+        if os.path.isdir(marathon_image_dir) and os.path.isdir(pmaports_community):
+            for marathon_aport in os.listdir(os.path.join(marathon_image_dir, "packages")):
+                if not marathon_aport.startswith("device-") or not marathon_aport.endswith("-marathon"):
+                    continue
+                src = os.path.join(marathon_image_dir, "packages", marathon_aport)
+                dst = os.path.join(pmaports_community, marathon_aport)
+                if os.path.islink(dst) or not os.path.exists(dst):
+                    if os.path.islink(dst):
+                        os.unlink(dst)
+                    subprocess.run(["cp", "-a", src, dst], check=True)
+                else:
+                    # rsync the contents; --delete so removed files in
+                    # Marathon-Image disappear from the pmaports copy too.
+                    subprocess.run(
+                        ["rsync", "-a", "--delete",
+                         os.path.join(src, ""), os.path.join(dst, "")],
+                        check=True,
+                    )
+
         # Make sure the pmaports cache has the right branch checked out. The mkosi
         # sandbox has no network access, so the configure script uses --skip-fetch
         resolved = resolve(device_name, ui_name, release)
-- 
